WEBVTT

00:02:03.791 --> 00:02:07.083
We're both girls, and yet...

00:02:18.541 --> 00:02:21.541
We're in Class B, Yamada! You're with me!

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.166
Thank goodness!

00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:26.625
TOMOKA KASE

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.958
Oh. I'm in Class B, too.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:45.500
We started dating not that long ago...

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:56.000
The weather has been overcast and a bit unpredictable

00:02:50.001 --> 00:02:56.000
lately, but it looks like change is in the air.

00:02:56.583 --> 00:03:00.333
Starting tomorrow, we can expect

00:02:56.584 --> 00:03:00.333
fair weather and clear skies.

00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:02.708
Going forward...

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:08.083
It's Kase-san!

00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:10.250
I-is everything okay?!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.375
Unread

00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:12.375
Today

00:03:10.252 --> 00:03:12.375
Are you free to talk?

00:03:10.253 --> 00:03:12.375
Enter message

00:03:17.041 --> 00:03:19.666
Yeah... Sure...

00:03:29.458 --> 00:03:31.541
Hello?! Yamada speaking!

00:03:31.541 --> 00:03:32.541
Uh...

00:03:32.541 --> 00:03:34.166
I know who you are.

00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:36.750
This is Kase, by the way.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:42.333
Yes, I know... Of course you are!

00:03:36.751 --> 00:03:42.333
I mean, I prepared myself for this!

00:03:43.208 --> 00:03:46.541
Why would you have to "prepare" yourself?

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:46.541
Anyway, what were you doing just now?

00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:50.625
Now? I took a bath earlier, and now I...

00:03:50.875 --> 00:03:53.541
Well, I'm reading a book about greenery!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.250
"Greenery"?

00:03:56.083 --> 00:03:57.083
Ah.

00:03:58.208 --> 00:03:59.458
By the way...

00:03:59.666 --> 00:04:01.000
Um, Kase-san?

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.500
Yeah, what?

00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:09.458
The truth is, I haven't... Well, I don't have

00:04:03.584 --> 00:04:09.458
much experience talking to boys.

00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:13.916
You're actually the first person I've ever dated.

00:04:14.666 --> 00:04:18.208
I-it's kind of embarrassing, right?

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:18.208
Seeing as how we're third-years and all.

00:04:18.208 --> 00:04:21.375
No, it's not embarrassing! Like, not at-

00:04:21.375 --> 00:04:22.041
Oh.

00:04:21.376 --> 00:04:22.041
Still...

00:04:22.041 --> 00:04:26.583
couples usually go out on dates and stuff, right?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:34.375
What was that just now?! H-hello? Hello? Oh, no!

00:04:35.166 --> 00:04:36.708
Uh, don't worry. It's nothing.

00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:36.708
Are you okay?

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:39.125
You sound like you're out of breath, Kase-san!

00:04:39.125 --> 00:04:43.166
I know your training is important,

00:04:39.126 --> 00:04:43.166
but you can't overdo it! Kase-san?

00:04:43.541 --> 00:04:45.875
I'm fine. Seriously, no problem.

00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:48.291
Oh, really? Thank goodness.

00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:53.333
So, what SPECIFICALLY would you like me to do?

00:04:57.083 --> 00:04:58.125
Uh...

00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:00.875
Hello? Kase-san? Kase-san?!

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.625
Y-Yamada...

00:05:04.791 --> 00:05:06.916
Just do whatever you want.

00:05:06.916 --> 00:05:09.250
Huh? Really, that's it?

00:05:09.916 --> 00:05:10.916
Yeah.

00:05:10.916 --> 00:05:12.333
Oh, jeez... Okay!

00:05:12.333 --> 00:05:15.041
Yeah. Well, good night.

00:05:38.666 --> 00:05:41.500
No, I DO want to! I do!

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.958
Will you... go out with me?

00:05:40.958 --> 00:05:44.916
Ah! It's fine, though, if you don't want to. I'm sorry.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:46.083
I've felt the same way about you, for so long.

00:05:46.208 --> 00:05:49.416
Just being with her is... it's like a dream!

00:05:52.458 --> 00:05:55.750
I love Kase-san, and she loves me!

00:05:56.625 --> 00:05:58.375
I don't know what to do with myself!

00:06:01.708 --> 00:06:03.833
Just do whatever you want.

00:06:05.833 --> 00:06:11.000
Dating someone isn't as clear-cut as I'd thought.

00:06:11.791 --> 00:06:14.416
Still, at times like this...

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:18.333
...a home-cooked lunch is the way to go!

00:06:16.666 --> 00:06:19.708
Cute

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:19.708
-n-

00:06:16.668 --> 00:06:19.708
Small

00:06:16.669 --> 00:06:19.708
Box Lunches

00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:30.791
Huh? Kase-san's out today?!

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:35.541
The track club needed her,

00:06:31.251 --> 00:06:35.541
so she said she'd be back later.

00:06:35.541 --> 00:06:37.291
So then, she IS out!

00:06:41.833 --> 00:06:43.625
I just want to go to sleep...

00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:44.958
What, THERE?

00:06:45.708 --> 00:06:51.833
Let's Plan for the School Trip

00:06:45.709 --> 00:06:51.833
-Daily Schedule

00:06:46.708 --> 00:06:49.416
It'll be my first time to Okinawa!

00:06:46.709 --> 00:06:49.416
And my first time on a plane!

00:06:49.416 --> 00:06:51.416
Okay, everyone, settle down.

00:06:51.833 --> 00:07:05.833
Let's Plan for the School Trip

00:06:51.834 --> 00:07:05.833
-Daily Schedule

00:06:51.835 --> 00:07:05.833
- What to bring

00:06:51.836 --> 00:07:05.833
-Duty Roster

00:06:51.958 --> 00:06:57.625
If you get all worked up now,

00:06:51.959 --> 00:06:57.625
you'll burn yourselves out before we even get there.

00:06:57.625 --> 00:06:59.833
We're YOUNG, so we'll be fine!

00:06:59.833 --> 00:07:01.416
Got that right!

00:07:02.125 --> 00:07:05.833
Could it be, ladies, that you're trying to provoke me?

00:07:07.791 --> 00:07:10.541
It's almost too much to take! Right, Yamada?

00:08:27.458 --> 00:08:28.250
YO!

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.750
Working hard again today, huh?

00:08:32.791 --> 00:08:34.583
Oh, jeez. Thanks a lot, Mikawa.

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:39.500
What's with you? You were sighing and stuff,

00:08:34.751 --> 00:08:39.500
so I thought I'd try to cheer you up.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:40.583
"Sighing"?

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.666
I was? Like, right now?

00:08:43.083 --> 00:08:44.416
Okay, well, see you.

00:08:44.583 --> 00:08:45.791
Bye!

00:08:46.041 --> 00:08:47.416
Uh, yeah.

00:08:49.708 --> 00:08:52.083
I was... sighing?

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.250
No! I have to get through this!

00:09:24.416 --> 00:09:26.166
Ah! Oh no, I sighed!

00:09:30.125 --> 00:09:32.416
Yamada! Good morning!

00:09:33.416 --> 00:09:34.958
Good morning, Kase-san!

00:09:35.291 --> 00:09:37.291
Um! Actually, I...

00:09:37.291 --> 00:09:38.916
Hold on a second. So, I-

00:09:38.916 --> 00:09:40.083
Good morning!

00:09:40.708 --> 00:09:42.541
Hey! What the heck are you doing?!

00:09:42.541 --> 00:09:44.541
It was SO boring with you gone yesterday!

00:09:44.541 --> 00:09:46.416
Let's all go to Class D together!

00:09:46.416 --> 00:09:50.500
Suzuki said she'd write that article

00:09:46.417 --> 00:09:50.500
for the club magazine, but it's not happening.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.708
Huh? She STILL hasn't done it yet?

00:09:52.708 --> 00:09:54.708
I told her to get on it, but she just...

00:09:55.416 --> 00:09:57.791
C'mon, Kase! You've gotta give her the smackdown!

00:09:57.791 --> 00:09:59.208
Yeah!

00:09:57.792 --> 00:09:59.208
That's right!

00:09:59.208 --> 00:10:00.625
Just do it! C'mon, please!

00:09:59.209 --> 00:10:00.625
The thing is, we...

00:10:00.625 --> 00:10:01.416
"Sorry."

00:10:07.291 --> 00:10:09.416
Kase-san sure is popular.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.208
Y-yeah.

00:10:14.041 --> 00:10:15.458
Well, I guess it's fine.

00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:17.916
I'll talk to her about it at lunch.

00:10:28.125 --> 00:10:30.083
Yamada! Let's eat already.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.291
Ah! Um, today, Kase-san and I were going to-

00:10:33.291 --> 00:10:36.625
Huh? Kase-san already went to the cafeteria

00:10:33.292 --> 00:10:36.625
with the Track Club.

00:10:36.958 --> 00:10:37.833
What?!

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.791
You're sleeping AGAIN?

00:11:01.375 --> 00:11:03.375
Yamada-san, are you...

00:11:05.916 --> 00:11:07.458
Did you and Kase-san hook up?

00:11:09.583 --> 00:11:11.125
Wh-why would you ask that?!

00:11:11.125 --> 00:11:14.375
It was just a feeling. You even made lunch for her, so...

00:11:14.375 --> 00:11:16.541
Ah... Ah!

00:11:17.166 --> 00:11:20.458
U-um, this is, well...

00:11:25.708 --> 00:11:27.125
You should've told me!

00:11:27.916 --> 00:11:31.083
Sorry. It's just sort of, well...

00:11:36.666 --> 00:11:37.458
Here.

00:11:38.166 --> 00:11:43.083
I'm not one to talk, but it must be hard

00:11:38.167 --> 00:11:43.083
being with someone that popular.

00:11:51.208 --> 00:11:54.166
Still, that won't get you down, right?

00:12:03.125 --> 00:12:07.958
Huh? You're out already? Sorry!

00:12:03.126 --> 00:12:07.958
I'll get you another one next time!

00:12:17.833 --> 00:12:20.833
Front Gate

00:12:17.834 --> 00:12:20.833
Bicycle Parking

00:12:40.875 --> 00:12:42.666
Huh? How come you didn't finish this?

00:12:43.875 --> 00:12:45.041
Kase-san!

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:48.500
Delish!

00:13:05.541 --> 00:13:08.833
That was great! Thanks so much.

00:13:09.625 --> 00:13:14.000
My bad. It never hit me that you'd made me lunch.

00:13:15.125 --> 00:13:18.666
I'm always running around and never sitting still, so...

00:13:21.125 --> 00:13:25.000
No. You're kind, and really, really cool.

00:13:25.125 --> 00:13:28.041
It's no wonder everybody likes you.

00:13:30.875 --> 00:13:31.958
Yamada?

00:13:40.833 --> 00:13:46.333
Oh, yeah. I guess there've been

00:13:40.834 --> 00:13:46.333
lots of things like this I've never noticed...

00:13:46.333 --> 00:13:48.125
Things that are important.

00:13:56.791 --> 00:13:57.625
Let's go.

00:13:57.625 --> 00:13:58.750
Huh? Um...

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:03.916
This way!

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.833
Here. Take a look.

00:14:12.541 --> 00:14:13.791
The shrubbery...?

00:14:14.375 --> 00:14:18.791
When you were a 2nd-year,

00:14:14.376 --> 00:14:18.791
you'd tend to them during your free time, right?

00:14:18.791 --> 00:14:22.291
Even though I bet you had just

00:14:18.792 --> 00:14:22.291
10 minutes left after you'd eaten lunch.

00:14:30.375 --> 00:14:34.083
You'd look after them all, from one end to the next.

00:14:35.791 --> 00:14:40.583
You had that green umbrella for when it was raining,

00:14:35.792 --> 00:14:40.583
and wore a straw hat when it was sunny.

00:14:41.125 --> 00:14:44.000
I would watch, thinking how amazing you are...

00:14:44.708 --> 00:14:47.500
And hoping that, just maybe,

00:14:44.709 --> 00:14:47.500
you'd turn around and notice me.

00:14:56.666 --> 00:14:58.000
But you...

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:02.166
You never looked up, no matter how long I stared at you.

00:15:03.541 --> 00:15:05.083
What a creeper, right?

00:15:05.375 --> 00:15:11.666
I'm just some stalker! This WHOLE time,

00:15:05.376 --> 00:15:11.666
I've been stalking your greenery!

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:14.583
Kase-san...

00:15:15.125 --> 00:15:17.458
But our eyes finally met...

00:15:18.916 --> 00:15:20.083
Right here.

00:15:31.291 --> 00:15:35.708
Kase-san and I have been going out since spring.

00:15:41.166 --> 00:15:46.458
I like gardening, so I'm in the Horticulture Club,

00:15:41.167 --> 00:15:46.458
while Kase-san is the star of the Track Club,

00:15:46.458 --> 00:15:51.000
and has even competed three times

00:15:46.459 --> 00:15:51.000
in national tournaments.

00:15:53.416 --> 00:15:57.083
She's the first person I've ever gone out with.

00:15:57.666 --> 00:16:00.166
That's more important than the fact we're both girls.

00:17:35.291 --> 00:17:40.500
I love her so much, I don't know what to do with myself.

00:18:04.333 --> 00:18:06.583
Yamada, are you free today?

00:18:06.583 --> 00:18:07.500
Huh?

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:11.750
Turns out we're only having a club meeting today,

00:18:07.501 --> 00:18:11.750
so I think I can leave early.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.791
Oh, really? That almost never happens!

00:18:13.958 --> 00:18:15.166
So, you want to come over?

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.375
Huh? Is that okay?!

00:18:19.375 --> 00:18:25.458
Yup! My parents will be getting home late today,

00:18:19.376 --> 00:18:25.458
and I figured I'd get lonely on my own, so...

00:18:25.458 --> 00:18:28.458
O-oh. Well, I guess that'd be okay.

00:18:28.458 --> 00:18:29.750
Woo-hoo!

00:18:32.083 --> 00:18:35.791
S-so, I'll just drop this stuff off at my place first.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.291
Sure! See you later, okay?

00:18:38.291 --> 00:18:39.541
See- Ow!

00:18:39.541 --> 00:18:40.541
Kase-san?

00:18:41.833 --> 00:18:44.083
Yeah. I'm fine, no worries!

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.000
What suddenly got into her?

00:18:47.666 --> 00:18:48.750
Huh...

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:54.375
Well, never mind. I need to hurry home and get ready!

00:18:55.458 --> 00:18:57.166
And now for the final check!

00:18:57.875 --> 00:19:00.791
No texts, and change to our meeting time.

00:19:01.125 --> 00:19:05.333
The room is nice and tidy, the desk's cleared up,

00:19:01.126 --> 00:19:05.333
and the fabrics look good!

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:10.916
Done and done! Now, all that's left

00:19:07.001 --> 00:19:10.916
is to wait for her to get here.

00:19:26.875 --> 00:19:29.750
Kase-san and I, alone together in my room...

00:19:30.666 --> 00:19:34.250
This is... this might be a big deal.

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:42.875
Yes...?

00:19:42.875 --> 00:19:44.458
H-hi there!

00:19:44.458 --> 00:19:45.625
Kase-san!

00:19:45.625 --> 00:19:47.583
Thank you for coming! Did you find it all right?

00:19:47.583 --> 00:19:48.916
Yeah, no problem.

00:19:49.208 --> 00:19:52.000
I checked the map a bunch of times, so I...!

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:56.333
The map? Oh, so I'm sure you were fine.

00:19:56.333 --> 00:19:58.333
Anyway, I bought THESE!

00:19:58.958 --> 00:19:59.916
Cakes?

00:19:59.916 --> 00:20:01.083
Let's eat them together.

00:20:01.833 --> 00:20:02.875
Yeah!

00:20:03.875 --> 00:20:06.583
It's a bit messy, but come on in.

00:20:06.583 --> 00:20:09.416
S-sorry for the bother...

00:20:13.083 --> 00:20:15.041
I feel a little embarrassed...

00:20:29.208 --> 00:20:30.000
Here!

00:20:30.833 --> 00:20:32.208
Uh... What?

00:20:32.208 --> 00:20:34.333
I'll make us some tea, so just have a seat.

00:20:34.333 --> 00:20:35.750
Oh. Okay.

00:20:40.791 --> 00:20:43.458
Kase-san is in my room!

00:20:51.916 --> 00:20:54.125
It's really kind of embarrassing!

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:57.583
But I'm so happy.

00:21:00.416 --> 00:21:01.333
Sorry for the wait.

00:21:05.708 --> 00:21:07.708
What's wrong? Are you feeling sick or-?

00:21:07.708 --> 00:21:09.333
No, I'm fine!

00:21:09.541 --> 00:21:11.791
I was just thinking, your bed is so fluffy!

00:21:12.041 --> 00:21:13.916
O-oh, so that's it.

00:21:16.416 --> 00:21:18.750
You sure have a lot of books in here...

00:21:19.291 --> 00:21:21.041
Oh. This one's all in English.

00:21:21.458 --> 00:21:26.000
It's published by the National Trust,

00:21:21.459 --> 00:21:26.000
a conservational charity in the UK.

00:21:26.625 --> 00:21:27.583
Huh...

00:21:27.583 --> 00:21:30.083
England is a kind of mecca for gardeners.

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:33.208
I'd like to go there someday.

00:21:33.208 --> 00:21:36.291
What?! Yamada, you're going to England? For life?

00:21:36.291 --> 00:21:41.333
Huh? No, no way. I can't even speak English!

00:21:36.292 --> 00:21:41.333
I just thought it'd be nice to visit.

00:21:44.375 --> 00:21:46.041
You're pretty amazing, you know.

00:21:46.375 --> 00:21:49.583
What? I'm really not...

00:21:46.376 --> 00:21:49.583
Anyway, let's have some cake! Okay?

00:21:54.375 --> 00:21:55.583
They're shortcakes!

00:21:59.041 --> 00:22:01.000
Here, Yamada. You can have mine.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.166
You like these, right?

00:22:02.833 --> 00:22:07.000
Huh? Y-yes, I do, but it's the strawberry

00:22:02.834 --> 00:22:07.000
that makes the cake.

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:10.166
Oh, cut it out. Just say "Aah."

00:22:14.583 --> 00:22:15.541
Aah!

00:22:17.041 --> 00:22:18.166
Is it good?

00:22:18.375 --> 00:22:19.375
Yup, yup!

00:22:33.625 --> 00:22:35.875
I'll sit and eat here, too!

00:22:38.125 --> 00:22:40.708
You sure do like strawberry shortcake, huh?

00:22:49.666 --> 00:22:50.416
Yamada...

00:22:50.416 --> 00:22:51.291
Hm?

00:22:52.083 --> 00:22:54.375
Are you...? That is...

00:22:55.166 --> 00:22:56.375
You and me...

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:00.291
You're okay doing this? With me?

00:23:00.791 --> 00:23:01.833
Hm?

00:23:05.583 --> 00:23:06.791
Well...?

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:09.333
Does she mean, kissing?

00:23:10.041 --> 00:23:11.791
Maybe she means a kiss.

00:23:14.083 --> 00:23:15.583
Um, well...

00:23:19.958 --> 00:23:21.500
Yeah. Yes. I am.

00:23:22.666 --> 00:23:25.166
If YOU want to, that is.

00:23:28.958 --> 00:23:32.041
Ah! Just give me a minute. I want to drink this first.

00:23:32.916 --> 00:23:34.041
O-ow!

00:23:41.583 --> 00:23:43.958
Yamada... You don't get it, do you?

00:23:46.416 --> 00:23:51.333
Sorry. I guess I got the wrong idea

00:23:46.417 --> 00:23:51.333
when you invited me over.

00:23:52.125 --> 00:23:53.791
No! I-I do get it!

00:23:53.791 --> 00:23:55.583
Don't lie. You don't understand.

00:23:55.583 --> 00:23:58.791
I'm not lying! And I DO understand, for real!

00:23:58.791 --> 00:24:00.166
Kase-san, I want to be with-

00:24:05.708 --> 00:24:07.541
Do you, Yamada?

00:24:08.208 --> 00:24:12.291
Because I want us to be together. Like, for real.

00:24:12.291 --> 00:24:13.458
"For real"?

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:15.500
What does that...?

00:24:23.333 --> 00:24:28.250
Kase-san smells so good... Like that herb, an aromatic.

00:24:28.875 --> 00:24:31.291
Huh? What was it called...?

00:24:38.833 --> 00:24:42.875
Mom

00:24:38.834 --> 00:24:42.875
Cell Phone

00:24:43.041 --> 00:24:44.250
Hello?

00:24:45.500 --> 00:24:47.291
Yes, I'm home.

00:24:47.583 --> 00:24:51.708
Oh. Yes. I'm here with a friend. And she brought cake!

00:24:52.208 --> 00:24:55.708
Huh? Did I "thank" her? Yes, of course I did!

00:24:55.916 --> 00:24:58.625
Yes. I know already, jeez!

00:24:59.125 --> 00:25:02.708
Yeah. Okay. See you then.

00:25:09.083 --> 00:25:12.875
Oh... That was my mom. She said she'll be home soon.

00:25:15.416 --> 00:25:16.750
Wh-what?

00:25:16.750 --> 00:25:20.250
That freaked me out! Is your volume set on MAX or what?

00:25:20.250 --> 00:25:22.208
Huh? I-I don't think so.

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:24.416
Oh. I guess it was...

00:25:24.416 --> 00:25:25.291
Yamada.

00:25:25.625 --> 00:25:27.208
Come here. Have a seat.

00:25:40.583 --> 00:25:41.291
Ow!

00:25:41.291 --> 00:25:42.375
Body slam!

00:25:46.875 --> 00:25:48.583
We can do this again next time.

00:25:48.583 --> 00:25:50.166
"N-next time"?

00:25:51.166 --> 00:25:54.000
I can't believe I got to leave school early today!

00:25:55.583 --> 00:25:59.583
I'm so happy... I might not be able to sleep tonight!

00:26:02.541 --> 00:26:06.625
Before I forget, are you wearing perfume?

00:26:02.542 --> 00:26:06.625
You smell REALLY good.

00:26:07.041 --> 00:26:09.500
I-I'm sorry! I stink? Like, sweat?

00:26:09.500 --> 00:26:14.500
No, NO! Not at all. Just now,

00:26:09.501 --> 00:26:14.500
I smelled something faint but really nice.

00:26:14.916 --> 00:26:17.833
Like an herb... Lemongrass!

00:26:17.833 --> 00:26:19.500
Lemon? Oh.

00:26:20.708 --> 00:26:21.791
Maybe it was this.

00:26:22.458 --> 00:26:26.666
I use this after practice.

00:26:22.459 --> 00:26:26.666
It's a body spray. Give me your hand.

00:26:26.791 --> 00:26:27.625
Okay.

00:26:29.666 --> 00:26:34.000
Wow, that's cold! Ah! But, yes, this is what I smelled!

00:26:34.166 --> 00:26:35.333
It's like lemongrass!

00:26:47.291 --> 00:26:51.083
Can I stay like this... for just a little while, Yamada?

00:26:57.541 --> 00:27:04.791
That scent of lemongrass... It lingered for so long.

00:27:15.250 --> 00:27:18.500
Our estimated arrival time

00:27:15.251 --> 00:27:18.500
at Naha Airport will be 10:00 AM.

00:27:20.125 --> 00:27:21.833
That's the sky!

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:24.625
We're flying! Look, this plane is flying!

00:27:24.625 --> 00:27:27.000
And they even gave us DRINKS!

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:30.166
I can't take it... Flying is so much fun!

00:27:31.250 --> 00:27:32.583
Hey, Mikawatchi...

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:35.750
Huh? Um, you can take off your seat belt now.

00:27:36.083 --> 00:27:40.500
I don't want to take it off...

00:27:36.084 --> 00:27:40.500
But I think there may be reason for me to-!

00:27:41.291 --> 00:27:43.166
Mikawatchi? Are you all right?

00:27:43.166 --> 00:27:44.333
G-gotta use the toilet!

00:27:44.333 --> 00:27:45.208
Okay...

00:27:46.666 --> 00:27:48.250
I hope she's okay.

00:27:48.583 --> 00:27:50.500
Whoa! This thing is SUPER tropical!

00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:51.458
What, what is?

00:27:51.458 --> 00:27:54.041
It's a blend of tropical orange and black tea, and it rocks!

00:27:54.583 --> 00:27:55.750
What are you talkin' about?

00:27:55.750 --> 00:27:56.666
For real! Like, seriously!

00:27:56.666 --> 00:27:57.750
Fine, then give me some!

00:28:00.166 --> 00:28:02.500
I can't handle this sort of thing...

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:05.500
Maybe some music will drown them out...

00:28:05.500 --> 00:28:08.375
The hell? If you think I'm lying, just try some!

00:28:08.375 --> 00:28:10.583
Dude, shut up. Fine, lemme try some.

00:28:11.250 --> 00:28:11.916
Do it!

00:28:12.291 --> 00:28:13.416
This has gotta suck.

00:28:14.833 --> 00:28:15.875
Nah, for real...!

00:28:17.041 --> 00:28:20.375
Hey. Let's go, Yamada. I wanna show you something.

00:28:20.375 --> 00:28:22.416
K..Kase-san!

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:25.958
Ah! Um, Kase-san?

00:28:25.958 --> 00:28:27.791
This is it. Here, look.

00:28:33.250 --> 00:28:34.208
Right? Pretty great, don't-?

00:28:34.208 --> 00:28:36.083
It's great! It's SO great!

00:28:36.750 --> 00:28:40.333
It's always sunny above the clouds.

00:28:36.751 --> 00:28:40.333
Did you know that, Kase-san?

00:28:40.333 --> 00:28:43.916
Huh? Y-yeah. I guess I did...

00:28:43.916 --> 00:28:50.000
Even on bad days, when I'm feeling down

00:28:43.917 --> 00:28:50.000
or when one of my flowers wilts...

00:28:50.208 --> 00:28:53.208
I know that it's always,

00:28:50.209 --> 00:28:53.208
always sunny up above the clouds.

00:28:53.416 --> 00:28:58.000
When I think about that, it gives me the strength

00:28:53.417 --> 00:28:58.000
to keep doing my best! You know?!

00:29:03.291 --> 00:29:05.083
Yes. I do.

00:29:08.916 --> 00:29:16.000
The other day, when I took first place in the regional

00:29:08.917 --> 00:29:16.000
prelims, someone from another team filed a complaint.

00:29:16.791 --> 00:29:22.083
The girl in the next lane fell,

00:29:16.792 --> 00:29:22.083
and they thought that I'd tripped her.

00:29:22.375 --> 00:29:26.500
We fought the decision,

00:29:22.376 --> 00:29:26.500
and finally got to do the race over...

00:29:27.250 --> 00:29:30.166
It didn't change anything, though.

00:29:30.958 --> 00:29:33.625
Everyone just wants to win. I get that.

00:29:36.541 --> 00:29:38.500
But still...

00:29:39.416 --> 00:29:40.375
Anyway.

00:29:41.208 --> 00:29:43.958
When I look out at this sky, none of that matters.

00:29:44.291 --> 00:29:48.375
Whatever happens, it's always sunny up here. Right?

00:30:12.458 --> 00:30:16.125
Wow! The sky is so different here!

00:30:16.958 --> 00:30:19.833
And the hibiscus is already blooming!

00:30:20.458 --> 00:30:22.083
Makes you glad to have been born...

00:30:22.083 --> 00:30:23.541
Mikawatchi! Say "cheese"!

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:27.041
Why'd you have to go taking my picture?!

00:30:27.041 --> 00:30:29.166
I-I'm glad you're feeling better, at least.

00:30:29.291 --> 00:30:30.833
Edit

00:30:30.916 --> 00:30:32.416
She's so cute...

00:30:35.708 --> 00:30:37.500
I feel alive again!

00:30:38.708 --> 00:30:39.833
Here, Yamada.

00:30:42.625 --> 00:30:44.125
It's so good!

00:30:46.625 --> 00:30:48.250
Oh, sorry! Here.

00:30:50.583 --> 00:30:52.000
It's sweet and sour!

00:30:57.916 --> 00:30:58.625
Cheese.

00:30:58.958 --> 00:31:00.500
Mikawa! When did you-?

00:31:00.500 --> 00:31:04.416
Never mind that. I'll take your picture for you!

00:31:06.125 --> 00:31:07.791
Okay, say "Cheese"!

00:31:10.541 --> 00:31:13.500
Yamada, let's buy something that matches.

00:31:13.500 --> 00:31:17.958
Yeah! Like, something small we can always carry around.

00:31:17.958 --> 00:31:19.416
Wow, you're such a girl.

00:31:19.750 --> 00:31:21.500
What's wrong with being a girl?

00:31:21.500 --> 00:31:23.000
It's neither good nor bad.

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:24.458
What does that mean?!

00:31:25.583 --> 00:31:26.916
Oh! Look, it's Kase-san!

00:31:27.708 --> 00:31:30.583
Hey, help us choose some souvenirs

00:31:27.709 --> 00:31:30.583
for the junior students!

00:31:30.583 --> 00:31:33.625
Ah. Okay, I'm coming.

00:31:33.625 --> 00:31:35.208
Sorry. I'll get with you later.

00:31:35.375 --> 00:31:36.291
Sure.

00:31:38.416 --> 00:31:42.166
Kase-san and I have different hotel rooms...

00:31:43.375 --> 00:31:45.166
Look! Now THAT'S an ocean view!

00:31:45.375 --> 00:31:47.500
And this bed is mine!

00:31:47.500 --> 00:31:48.291
Hey, that's not fair!

00:31:48.291 --> 00:31:50.708
I can see the beach, right from my fluffy bed!

00:31:50.916 --> 00:31:52.250
Yay~!

00:31:52.250 --> 00:31:53.541
Jeez...

00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:55.791
I'm glad to be with Mikawatchi...

00:31:56.166 --> 00:32:00.125
I'm gonna

00:31:56.167 --> 00:32:00.125
go take a bath!

00:31:56.168 --> 00:31:59.750
But honestly, I wish I could've stayed with Kase-san.

00:32:00.125 --> 00:32:02.083
BATH

00:32:01.958 --> 00:32:03.708
Nice! There's no one here!

00:32:03.708 --> 00:32:05.916
Wow, it's so pretty!

00:32:08.583 --> 00:32:11.250
Kase-san

00:32:08.584 --> 00:32:11.250
On my way.

00:32:18.625 --> 00:32:20.250
Huh?! What gives?!

00:32:21.041 --> 00:32:23.291
So, what did you buy them?

00:32:23.291 --> 00:32:25.250
Huh? "Chinsu..." something-or-other.

00:32:25.250 --> 00:32:28.458
T... Taking a bath with Kase-san is just-

00:32:28.458 --> 00:32:32.416
It's too late to say that NOW. Anyway, I'm going in!

00:32:33.333 --> 00:32:35.458
This tub is super huge, right?

00:32:35.458 --> 00:32:36.833
Okay, let's have a race!

00:32:36.833 --> 00:32:38.125
Hey, quit swimming!

00:32:48.041 --> 00:32:51.291
Yamada... It's hard for you

00:32:48.042 --> 00:32:51.291
to take a bath with me here, isn't it?

00:32:53.916 --> 00:32:58.333
I'm used to it, changing and showering

00:32:53.917 --> 00:32:58.333
with my other track members, but...

00:32:59.291 --> 00:33:04.583
if you feel uncomfortable, I-I'll make sure not to look.

00:33:04.583 --> 00:33:06.416
Kase! Are you coming or what?

00:33:06.416 --> 00:33:08.083
I'm the queen of the bath, girl!

00:33:08.416 --> 00:33:09.625
I told you not to swim!

00:33:09.625 --> 00:33:11.083
Shut up already!

00:33:11.375 --> 00:33:12.750
I'll be right there.

00:33:18.916 --> 00:33:20.875
I'm going in, okay?

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:33.625
I-I'll just take a bath in our room...

00:33:50.500 --> 00:33:52.375
Let's hook up

00:33:50.501 --> 00:33:52.375
during free time tomorrow, yeah?

00:33:52.666 --> 00:33:53.916
Um, well...

00:33:56.708 --> 00:33:58.750
Let's just talk about it tomorrow.

00:34:00.125 --> 00:34:01.625
Yeah. Tomorrow.

00:34:03.708 --> 00:34:06.291
Jeez, I'm such a...!

00:34:07.250 --> 00:34:09.208
Read

00:34:07.251 --> 00:34:09.208
On my way.

00:34:07.252 --> 00:34:09.208
Read

00:34:07.253 --> 00:34:09.208
Let's hook up

00:34:07.254 --> 00:34:09.208
during free time tomorrow, yeah?

00:34:09.541 --> 00:34:12.208
What gives, Yamada?

00:34:16.375 --> 00:34:21.291
So, starting now, you'll be spending free time

00:34:16.376 --> 00:34:21.291
in your groups. Make sure you don't get lost.

00:34:21.708 --> 00:34:23.041
Okay, dismissed!

00:34:58.000 --> 00:34:59.083
Come with me.

00:34:59.416 --> 00:35:00.708
Um... What?

00:35:20.750 --> 00:35:23.625
Quit crying already, Yamada.

00:35:26.541 --> 00:35:28.500
Are you dumping me?

00:35:29.083 --> 00:35:30.000
Huh?

00:35:30.166 --> 00:35:35.291
I feel like, after you saw me naked,

00:35:30.167 --> 00:35:35.291
you've sort of hated me.

00:35:36.041 --> 00:35:39.291
It happens sometimes. You can be friends with someone,

00:35:39.291 --> 00:35:42.625
but after changing in front of each other for PE

00:35:39.292 --> 00:35:42.625
or whatever, they just become distant.

00:35:43.791 --> 00:35:46.000
I thought for sure that's what you-

00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:46.666
You're wrong!

00:35:47.666 --> 00:35:51.083
I just... I was surprised, that's all.

00:35:51.625 --> 00:35:52.541
Huh?

00:35:52.541 --> 00:35:56.958
I've only ever seen you with your clothes on, and I...

00:35:57.750 --> 00:36:00.833
I'm nothing but flab, so I got really embarrassed!

00:36:01.208 --> 00:36:04.250
There's no way I could be in a bath with you!

00:36:05.083 --> 00:36:09.791
I'm sorry you got the wrong idea, Kase-san. I'm so sorry!

00:36:16.500 --> 00:36:17.958
Kase-san?

00:36:18.541 --> 00:36:19.958
Oh, jeez...

00:36:20.458 --> 00:36:22.708
Thank goodness!

00:36:55.625 --> 00:36:57.500
Let's come here again.

00:36:57.500 --> 00:36:58.291
Huh?

00:36:58.458 --> 00:37:00.958
To Okinawa. But just you and me next time.

00:37:02.541 --> 00:37:03.666
Yeah!

00:37:10.708 --> 00:37:11.916
It's a promise.

00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:24.541
The coral that Kase-san and I found

00:37:19.001 --> 00:37:24.541
had the scent of summer...

00:37:36.166 --> 00:37:43.166
We'll be seeing clouds and rain all this week,

00:37:36.167 --> 00:37:43.166
so be sure to take an umbrella with you when going out.

00:37:41.250 --> 00:37:43.166
Hello? Oh, yes.

00:37:44.208 --> 00:37:45.500
It's been a while.

00:37:46.458 --> 00:37:49.875
Um, we're actually about to talk about it right now.

00:37:50.291 --> 00:37:54.958
Yes. I swear... I'm already nervous, Senpai.

00:37:58.416 --> 00:38:02.458
I think Yamada-san could easily

00:37:58.417 --> 00:38:02.458
get into Seigyoku University.

00:38:02.458 --> 00:38:03.666
Oh, really?

00:38:04.291 --> 00:38:07.416
She'd be in for sure if she could improve

00:38:04.292 --> 00:38:07.416
her English a bit more.

00:38:07.416 --> 00:38:11.125
Thank you so much. You'll have to study harder, Yui.

00:38:13.041 --> 00:38:14.041
Yeah...

00:38:19.833 --> 00:38:20.541
Ah!

00:38:32.791 --> 00:38:35.750
Special Film Screening

00:38:32.792 --> 00:38:35.750
"Melody" 1971

00:38:37.750 --> 00:38:39.208
Yamada!

00:38:39.208 --> 00:38:40.250
Kase-san!

00:38:43.500 --> 00:38:46.833
I saw you in the hallway earlier.

00:38:43.501 --> 00:38:46.833
Did you finish up with the counselor?

00:38:47.000 --> 00:38:48.041
Yeah...

00:38:56.791 --> 00:39:00.458
I've decided to... try for Nikkyo University.

00:39:00.916 --> 00:39:03.166
O-oh, really?

00:39:03.875 --> 00:39:07.583
Still, even with a recommendation,

00:39:03.876 --> 00:39:07.583
I might fail the entrance exam.

00:39:07.583 --> 00:39:10.000
Th-that's not true! You can do it, Kase-san!

00:39:10.250 --> 00:39:11.625
I'm not so sure...

00:39:11.625 --> 00:39:12.708
Well, I am!

00:39:15.041 --> 00:39:17.291
Anyway, how did yours go?

00:39:17.291 --> 00:39:18.083
Ah.

00:39:19.416 --> 00:39:20.375
Yeah...

00:39:20.833 --> 00:39:23.083
Which one did you go for? What school?

00:39:26.500 --> 00:39:28.791
In the end, I went with something local.

00:39:33.916 --> 00:39:39.166
Seigyoku Women's University.

00:39:33.917 --> 00:39:39.166
My parents say it's an easy commute... back home.

00:39:39.541 --> 00:39:41.250
Oh. I see.

00:39:42.125 --> 00:39:46.041
I don't think I could pack up

00:39:42.126 --> 00:39:46.041
and move somewhere else either, so I-

00:39:46.041 --> 00:39:48.625
That's great! Seigyoku is a good school.

00:39:48.958 --> 00:39:51.250
I think it'll suit you. Yeah.

00:39:51.833 --> 00:39:53.750
Plus, there's a lot of greenery around there.

00:39:54.791 --> 00:39:55.791
Yeah.

00:39:55.791 --> 00:39:56.625
So, what?

00:39:56.875 --> 00:40:00.000
The Horticulture Club works even in the rain?

00:40:00.583 --> 00:40:04.458
Come rain or shine, there are no days off for gardening!

00:40:04.458 --> 00:40:06.041
Okay! Then, I'll help!

00:40:06.041 --> 00:40:07.416
Huh? But, your umbrella!

00:40:07.416 --> 00:40:08.375
Don't need one!

00:40:08.375 --> 00:40:09.375
Over there is-

00:40:09.375 --> 00:40:10.208
Hydrangea, right?

00:40:10.208 --> 00:40:11.083
Yes!

00:40:15.500 --> 00:40:17.916
Wh-where should we put it?

00:40:17.916 --> 00:40:20.541
Next to that red pot over there.

00:40:20.541 --> 00:40:22.708
Okay. One, two...

00:40:22.708 --> 00:40:23.708
One, two!

00:40:27.333 --> 00:40:31.625
Those flowers sure are lucky.

00:40:27.334 --> 00:40:31.625
I wish you could help ME grow, too.

00:40:31.625 --> 00:40:32.375
Huh?

00:40:33.291 --> 00:40:35.000
Wh-what are you talking about?

00:40:35.375 --> 00:40:41.500
I'd like you to protect me from weeds

00:40:35.376 --> 00:40:41.500
and bugs and stuff, and give me water...

00:40:41.916 --> 00:40:43.875
That way, I'd get big and strong!

00:40:44.083 --> 00:40:45.875
Kase-san, what are you saying?!

00:40:47.916 --> 00:40:50.708
Sounds good, right? I'd like to be a flower.

00:40:50.708 --> 00:40:52.458
Wait, the rain! You'll get wet!

00:41:00.375 --> 00:41:01.541
A flower, huh?

00:41:03.166 --> 00:41:08.250
I think Kase-san is a lot like a flower...

00:41:09.041 --> 00:41:12.041
And the one she's most like is a sunflower.

00:41:12.500 --> 00:41:16.583
Because it grows big and tall,

00:41:12.501 --> 00:41:16.583
reaching straight for the sun.

00:41:25.250 --> 00:41:26.541
Say, Yamada...

00:41:26.541 --> 00:41:27.375
Hm?

00:41:27.625 --> 00:41:29.625
Why the literature department?

00:41:29.958 --> 00:41:32.875
Oh. Well, um...

00:41:34.083 --> 00:41:35.625
Ah! Sorry, gimme a sec.

00:41:35.625 --> 00:41:36.875
Yes, hello?

00:41:37.666 --> 00:41:40.708
Yeah. That's where I've decided to go.

00:41:41.625 --> 00:41:43.208
Huh? Okay.

00:41:44.625 --> 00:41:45.833
Wait, really?

00:41:46.208 --> 00:41:46.958
Ah.

00:41:47.500 --> 00:41:49.041
I'm with a friend right now.

00:41:49.708 --> 00:41:51.166
Let's talk about this tonight.

00:41:58.958 --> 00:42:00.125
Well, see you tomorrow!

00:42:01.333 --> 00:42:02.916
Oh. Yeah.

00:42:03.833 --> 00:42:04.875
See you.

00:42:11.333 --> 00:42:13.458
Why the literature department?

00:42:17.083 --> 00:42:20.708
Whoa, you went with Seigyoku University?

00:42:22.041 --> 00:42:23.958
So you're staying here after all?

00:42:24.500 --> 00:42:25.958
Yeah, I guess...

00:42:26.125 --> 00:42:27.708
What about you?

00:42:27.708 --> 00:42:31.291
Well, I'll go with whoever takes me.

00:42:31.291 --> 00:42:33.208
Whoa! Talk about random!

00:42:33.208 --> 00:42:36.583
Admissions Guide

00:42:33.209 --> 00:42:36.583
Seigyoku University

00:42:33.375 --> 00:42:36.458
Well, my life is mine to live!

00:42:51.666 --> 00:42:53.875
Are you sure about this, Yamada? Like, for real?

00:42:53.333 --> 00:42:55.416
Name: Zephyranthes

00:42:53.334 --> 00:42:55.416
Found with Yamada.

00:42:53.335 --> 00:42:55.416
-For those seeking

00:42:53.336 --> 00:42:55.416
to succeed in track and field

00:42:53.337 --> 00:42:55.416
-Includes menu and training tips

00:42:53.338 --> 00:42:55.416
from pro coaches

00:42:55.500 --> 00:42:56.875
What do you mean?

00:42:56.875 --> 00:43:01.375
Kase-san! She got an athletics recommendation

00:42:56.876 --> 00:43:01.375
to a school in Tokyo.

00:43:01.375 --> 00:43:02.625
You know that, right?

00:43:03.750 --> 00:43:06.083
Taking a test doesn't make it said and done!

00:43:06.083 --> 00:43:08.041
Of course it does!

00:43:08.250 --> 00:43:09.625
No, you're wrong!

00:43:19.708 --> 00:43:22.416
Third-years may drop out of their clubs in the summer,

00:43:23.166 --> 00:43:26.208
but Kase-san is going to keep on running, right?

00:43:26.208 --> 00:43:28.083
Face facts, Yamada!

00:43:28.083 --> 00:43:31.958
Nope, not listening! Can't hear you!

00:43:33.333 --> 00:43:36.041
What will you do if she goes to Tokyo?

00:43:36.750 --> 00:43:39.458
How can I...? Nothing's for sure yet.

00:43:39.458 --> 00:43:40.833
I swear!

00:43:40.833 --> 00:43:43.958
Still, that's how things go, I guess.

00:43:43.958 --> 00:43:44.708
Huh?

00:43:45.083 --> 00:43:48.958
You and I met in our first year of high school.

00:43:48.958 --> 00:43:51.500
We didn't know each other before then, right?

00:43:53.625 --> 00:43:54.833
Oh, yeah.

00:43:55.041 --> 00:43:59.250
We've been following the same pattern,

00:43:55.042 --> 00:43:59.250
over and over, since middle school.

00:43:59.458 --> 00:44:00.541
Yeah.

00:44:00.541 --> 00:44:05.000
And when we're at college, we'll have new encounters

00:44:00.542 --> 00:44:05.000
ahead of us... That goes for Kase-san as well.

00:44:05.916 --> 00:44:07.125
See? Look over there.

00:44:07.125 --> 00:44:09.416
Come on. Cut it out, Kase!

00:44:10.875 --> 00:44:13.666
You say that, but it looks like you're having fun.

00:44:13.666 --> 00:44:15.250
K..Kase-san?

00:44:13.667 --> 00:44:15.250
Seriously, what's with you? Jeez!

00:44:15.250 --> 00:44:17.958
You're enjoying yourself, right? Just do it.

00:44:19.208 --> 00:44:20.166
Kase-san?

00:44:20.166 --> 00:44:21.833
Okay. Let's go.

00:44:22.458 --> 00:44:23.208
Yeah.

00:44:23.208 --> 00:44:25.625
Kase-san! Don't go!

00:44:47.708 --> 00:44:49.500
Okay, see you later...

00:44:49.500 --> 00:44:51.833
Wait! Yui, you forgot your bag.

00:44:51.833 --> 00:44:52.791
Huh?

00:44:53.250 --> 00:44:55.458
Pull yourself together already.

00:45:03.291 --> 00:45:04.708
G'morning, Kase!

00:45:05.291 --> 00:45:07.250
Morning training again? You're SO busy!

00:45:07.250 --> 00:45:09.083
G'morning. Ah!

00:45:09.500 --> 00:45:10.625
'Morning, Yamada.

00:45:10.875 --> 00:45:12.125
G-good morning.

00:45:26.333 --> 00:45:27.750
What...

00:45:28.708 --> 00:45:30.375
What am I doing?

00:45:35.208 --> 00:45:38.458
Once we graduate, we might not even see each other.

00:45:52.625 --> 00:45:54.375
But during that time...

00:45:59.125 --> 00:46:03.958
I want to talk to her, more and more.

00:46:11.208 --> 00:46:12.875
I want to always...

00:46:14.958 --> 00:46:16.791
I want to be with her, forever!

00:46:37.791 --> 00:46:39.000
Hello...?

00:46:39.000 --> 00:46:41.333
What's with you, Yamada...?

00:46:44.208 --> 00:46:44.958
Huh?

00:46:45.875 --> 00:46:48.375
Did I do something wrong?

00:46:50.083 --> 00:46:52.375
No, not... Not really.

00:46:54.166 --> 00:46:56.750
Is it because I'm going to Tokyo?

00:46:57.250 --> 00:46:58.458
That's not...!

00:46:58.791 --> 00:47:00.458
That's not it.

00:47:03.125 --> 00:47:04.333
I guess not, huh?

00:47:04.875 --> 00:47:07.791
I haven't even been accepted yet, so...

00:47:07.791 --> 00:47:10.750
B-but you will! You'll get in for sure!

00:47:11.000 --> 00:47:12.416
The thing is, Yamada...

00:47:13.416 --> 00:47:14.125
Yes?

00:47:14.458 --> 00:47:18.125
I don't want to be away from you.

00:47:20.458 --> 00:47:23.291
The other day... It was just too much.

00:47:25.083 --> 00:47:29.625
I told my coach I was turning down the recommendation,

00:47:25.084 --> 00:47:29.625
and I'd be going to a local school instead.

00:47:30.041 --> 00:47:31.291
A local one?

00:47:31.291 --> 00:47:36.000
It turned into this big meeting...

00:47:31.292 --> 00:47:36.000
They even called me to the principal's office.

00:47:36.625 --> 00:47:38.166
So that's what happened?

00:47:38.791 --> 00:47:43.041
I want to be with you, Yamada. I'm serious.

00:47:45.041 --> 00:47:46.416
And I...!

00:47:46.416 --> 00:47:52.750
Even if you DO go to Tokyo, I'll call you every day

00:47:46.417 --> 00:47:52.750
and I'll go see you whenever I can! So...

00:47:55.583 --> 00:47:57.541
Good luck on your test.

00:47:58.458 --> 00:47:59.833
Thank you, Yamada.

00:48:02.916 --> 00:48:04.000
Of course.

00:48:12.833 --> 00:48:15.708
Kase-san is leaving today.

00:48:28.250 --> 00:48:29.208
Ah!

00:48:29.416 --> 00:48:30.625
Kase-san!

00:48:33.250 --> 00:48:34.625
Your entrance exam is tomorrow, right?

00:48:34.625 --> 00:48:35.750
Yup. That it is.

00:48:36.208 --> 00:48:38.666
I'm about to take the night shinkansen to get there.

00:48:39.333 --> 00:48:41.208
Do your best out there in Tokyo!

00:48:41.208 --> 00:48:42.125
Thanks.

00:48:44.291 --> 00:48:46.541
The schoolyard seems sort of bigger...

00:48:46.541 --> 00:48:47.166
Huh?

00:48:47.958 --> 00:48:49.625
Oh. You noticed?

00:48:49.625 --> 00:48:52.125
Of course I did. I'm always looking at it!

00:48:53.166 --> 00:48:54.125
Thank you!

00:48:54.125 --> 00:48:56.333
You're the only one who'd say something like that!

00:49:00.125 --> 00:49:01.875
The Culture Festival is coming up,

00:49:01.875 --> 00:49:04.291
and the wind instrument and orchestral clubs

00:49:01.876 --> 00:49:04.291
could use the room, right?

00:49:04.500 --> 00:49:07.583
So, I thought I'd clear out some space for them.

00:49:08.041 --> 00:49:10.000
It seems like kind of a waste, though...

00:49:10.000 --> 00:49:12.875
Not at all. This space belongs to everyone!

00:49:15.541 --> 00:49:19.291
Yamada. You always tell me how great I am...

00:49:19.625 --> 00:49:22.791
But to me, you're the one who's great.

00:49:23.000 --> 00:49:23.750
Huh?

00:49:23.750 --> 00:49:24.875
You ARE great.

00:49:28.708 --> 00:49:29.708
Sorry.

00:49:30.208 --> 00:49:31.416
Hello?

00:49:32.125 --> 00:49:33.875
Oh, yes! I'm headed there now.

00:49:33.875 --> 00:49:39.458
Once we graduate,

00:49:33.876 --> 00:49:39.458
we'll have new encounters awaiting us.

00:49:35.250 --> 00:49:40.958
When will I get to Tokyo? Uh... Well, it's gonna take some time.

00:49:40.958 --> 00:49:44.375
But even once we're in college...

00:49:42.833 --> 00:49:44.375
I know, right?

00:49:48.791 --> 00:49:50.083
Okay, see you tonight.

00:49:52.083 --> 00:49:54.250
That was a friend of mine who lives over there.

00:49:54.250 --> 00:49:58.291
She said she'd meet me at Tokyo Station.

00:49:54.251 --> 00:49:58.291
She's SUPER nice!

00:49:58.291 --> 00:50:01.000
Oh, really? She sounds like a good friend.

00:50:01.791 --> 00:50:03.416
On that day...

00:50:03.875 --> 00:50:04.750
Okay, Yamada.

00:50:05.166 --> 00:50:06.125
Do your best, yeah?

00:50:06.125 --> 00:50:07.083
And you, too!

00:50:13.583 --> 00:50:16.875
...the setting sun was so beautiful.

00:50:45.416 --> 00:50:49.500
The school's been so quiet without Kase-san here...

00:50:51.708 --> 00:50:53.166
It's just empty.

00:51:05.416 --> 00:51:08.250
No! What's empty is...

00:51:11.041 --> 00:51:13.000
Bus Stop

00:51:11.042 --> 00:51:13.000
West High

00:51:11.416 --> 00:51:12.583
ME!

00:51:21.375 --> 00:51:23.291
I can't be away from Kase-san...

00:51:24.375 --> 00:51:27.041
I can't let her go!

00:51:31.500 --> 00:51:35.250
The train bound for Shin-Osaka and Tokyo

00:51:31.501 --> 00:51:35.250
will soon be departing.

00:51:36.708 --> 00:51:38.000
This is it, Kase.

00:51:38.625 --> 00:51:39.875
Do your best, okay?

00:51:39.875 --> 00:51:41.125
I will, Coach!

00:51:44.250 --> 00:51:46.375
Remember, you're getting off at the last stop.

00:51:46.375 --> 00:51:49.166
I'm not in elementary school anymore, Coach.

00:52:03.958 --> 00:52:05.125
I'm coming!

00:52:05.125 --> 00:52:06.041
Yamada?!

00:52:06.041 --> 00:52:07.875
I'm going to Tokyo, too!

00:52:08.875 --> 00:52:10.958
To be with you!

00:52:12.833 --> 00:52:14.166
Yamada!

00:52:14.541 --> 00:52:15.750
I'm coming!

00:52:31.875 --> 00:52:34.166
I can't bear to be without you!

00:52:34.500 --> 00:52:36.583
I need you, Kase-san!

00:52:36.583 --> 00:52:37.375
Yamada...

00:52:37.375 --> 00:52:38.583
I...

00:52:54.083 --> 00:52:55.291
I'm so happy.

00:53:10.541 --> 00:53:15.041
Hikaru ase, T-shirt, deatta koi

00:53:10.542 --> 00:53:15.041
Glistening sweat, a T-shirt, a love encounter

00:53:15.958 --> 00:53:21.208
Dare yori mo kagayaku kimi o mite

00:53:15.959 --> 00:53:21.208
Looking at you, shining brighter than anyone else

00:53:21.375 --> 00:53:25.958
Hajimete no kimochi o mitsuketa yo

00:53:21.376 --> 00:53:25.958
I've found a new feeling

00:53:26.750 --> 00:53:31.958
Arata na tabi ga hajimaru

00:53:26.751 --> 00:53:31.958
A new journey begins

00:53:32.166 --> 00:53:36.791
Ameagari, kimagure, aoi kaze

00:53:32.167 --> 00:53:36.791
The rain clears, a fresh breeze blows at random

00:53:37.458 --> 00:53:42.791
Tsuyoi hizashi, itsuka oikoshite

00:53:37.459 --> 00:53:42.791
And one day will overetake the sun's blinding rays,

00:53:43.000 --> 00:53:53.541
Kore kara egaiteku koi no iro, hajimari no page irodoru yo

00:53:43.001 --> 00:53:53.541
The color of a love about to be rendered stains the pages

00:53:53.791 --> 00:54:04.458
Uranai zasshi, futatsu no hoshi ni futari no mirai o kasanete miru no

00:53:53.792 --> 00:54:04.458
An astrology magazine - let's try layering two futures on two stars

00:54:04.583 --> 00:54:09.875
Kasabuta darake, torenai kokoro

00:54:04.584 --> 00:54:09.875
A heart that's nothing but scabs and can't be peeled

00:54:09.875 --> 00:54:15.250
Anata no yasashisa de fusagaru

00:54:09.876 --> 00:54:15.250
Is healed by your kindness

00:54:17.583 --> 00:54:23.333
Itsu no ma ni ka sukima aita, kokoro ga mitasareteku

00:54:17.584 --> 00:54:23.333
Before I know it, a gap opens and my heart is fulfilled

00:54:23.541 --> 00:54:28.291
Futo shita shunkan no sarigenai shigusa

00:54:23.542 --> 00:54:28.291
A casual gesture, done when least expected

00:54:28.291 --> 00:54:31.041
Itsu no hi ni ka yume o kataru

00:54:28.292 --> 00:54:31.041
One day, I will recount these dreams

00:54:31.041 --> 00:54:39.416
Anata no kao o zutto mitsumete itai, hohoende itai

00:54:31.042 --> 00:54:39.416
I want to always gaze at your face, to always smile

00:54:50.333 --> 00:54:55.000
Taisetsu na nanika o mamoru toki,

00:54:50.334 --> 00:54:55.000
If that first step can become bravery

00:54:55.708 --> 00:55:00.958
Fumidaseru ippo ga yuuki nara

00:54:55.709 --> 00:55:00.958
When protecting something important

00:55:01.208 --> 00:55:06.541
Kizutsuku koto kara nigedashite,

00:55:01.209 --> 00:55:06.541
I've run from things that could hurt me,

00:55:06.541 --> 00:55:11.791
Itsumo tada toomawari bakari

00:55:06.542 --> 00:55:11.791
Always taking the long way around

00:55:12.000 --> 00:55:17.416
Yukiba naku shita tsuyogari no kuse ga

00:55:12.001 --> 00:55:17.416
My habit of acting tough has left me with no place to go,

00:55:17.416 --> 00:55:22.625
Kokoro no naka de tomadotte iru yo

00:55:17.417 --> 00:55:22.625
And left my heart hesitant

00:55:22.833 --> 00:55:28.083
Hajimete shitta anata no omoi ni

00:55:22.834 --> 00:55:28.083
These feelings I have for you, for the first time,

00:55:28.250 --> 00:55:33.125
Kotoba yori namida afurete kuru

00:55:28.251 --> 00:55:33.125
Make tears rather than words spill forth

00:55:33.125 --> 00:55:38.833
Sukoshi haba no chigau ashi de ippozutsu arukou ne

00:55:33.126 --> 00:55:38.833
Let's walk one step at a time, with a slightly wider gait

00:55:38.833 --> 00:55:43.708
Futari de ayumu michi, dekobako no michi

00:55:38.834 --> 00:55:43.708
A path walked together, a downtrodden path

00:55:43.875 --> 00:55:49.583
Futatsu-ori no shiroi chizu ni, kisu chiisana ketsui o

00:55:43.876 --> 00:55:49.583
A blank map folded in half and a small measure of resolve

00:55:49.708 --> 00:55:55.000
Shoujiki ni ima tsutaeyou

00:55:49.709 --> 00:55:55.000
Let's state these now, earnestly

00:56:06.541 --> 00:56:11.125
Mimimoto de kikoeru futari no melody

00:56:06.542 --> 00:56:11.125
Our melody, heard close to the ear

00:56:11.875 --> 00:56:16.583
Afuredasu namida koraete

00:56:11.876 --> 00:56:16.583
Holding back tears that will spill forth

00:56:17.291 --> 00:56:21.916
Arikitari no kotoba, anata ni iu yo

00:56:17.292 --> 00:56:21.916
These ordinary words I say to you:

00:56:22.125 --> 00:56:27.041
"Kore kara zutto issho da yo ne..."

00:56:22.126 --> 00:56:27.041
"As of now, we'll always be together..."

00:56:27.041 --> 00:56:29.708
Osaekirenai kono kimochi ga

00:56:27.042 --> 00:56:29.708
I can't hold back these feelings

00:56:29.708 --> 00:56:37.708
25-ji no sora kara hikaru shizuku to shite furisosoida

00:56:29.709 --> 00:56:37.708
That rained down like droplets from the 1:00 am sky

00:56:37.791 --> 00:56:43.708
Ki ga tsuitara, kokoro no naka, yasashii kaze ga fuite

00:56:37.792 --> 00:56:43.708
Then, I noticed the gentle breeze blowing within my heart

00:56:43.708 --> 00:56:48.333
Asu e no tobira, sotto hiraku

00:56:43.709 --> 00:56:48.333
The door toward tomorrow opens softly

00:56:48.541 --> 00:56:54.291
Kotoba ga ima toki o koete eien o tsukinukeru

00:56:48.542 --> 00:56:54.291
Words now transcend time piercing eternity

00:56:54.416 --> 00:56:59.250
Ikutsu mo no kisetsu o toorisugite

00:56:54.417 --> 00:56:59.250
And going past several seasons

00:56:59.416 --> 00:57:05.250
Tadoritsuita futari no basho, nagasugita tabi no ato

00:56:59.417 --> 00:57:05.250
A place we've reached, together, following a long journey

00:57:05.250 --> 00:57:10.041
Chikatta ai o sodateyou

00:57:05.251 --> 00:57:10.041
Let's foster this love we've pledged to each other

00:57:30.125 --> 00:57:33.500
So... What about morning glories?

00:57:35.083 --> 00:57:38.375
Morning glories? They symbolize fleeting love.

00:57:38.375 --> 00:57:39.291
That's right.

00:57:41.083 --> 00:57:43.833
But there's another meaning. Do you know it?

00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:55.458
Kase-san and Morning Glories.

00:57:50.833 --> 00:57:52.458
An everlasting bond.
